.TH MDI "1"  "2020-08-26" "LinuxCNC Documentation" "The Enhanced Machine Controller"
.SH NAME
mdi \- Send G-code commands from the terminal to the running LinuxCNC
instance
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mdi [command]

.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBmdi\fR sends G-code commands to LinuxCNC.
With arguments it sends one command and exits; with none it starts an
interactive session in which G-code commands are sent to the interpreter and
machine feedback is displayed.
An empty line prints the current position instead of sending anything.
.PP
Operator messages the command produces — the reason a line was refused, and
any \fB(MSG,\.\.\.)\fR or \fB(DEBUG,\.\.\.)\fR output — are printed on standard
error.  They are read from the server's message list and are not acknowledged,
so a running GUI still shows them too.

.SH USAGE

 send a single command and exit
 mdi m2 s1400

 interactive session
 $mdi
 MDI> m3 s1000
 MDI> G0 X100
 MDI> ^D
 $

.SH "EXIT STATUS"
0 if every command was issued and executed without an error message,
1 otherwise (the machine refused the command, reported an interpreter error,
or could not be reached).

.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
\fBSTMAK_REST_URL\fR
Base URL of the stratuMAK server (default \fBhttp://127.0.0.1:5080\fR).
.TP
\fBSTMAK_TASK_INSTANCE\fR
Task instance to address (default \fBmilltask\fR).

.SH "SEE ALSO"
\fBLinuxCNC(1)\fR

Much more information about LinuxCNC and HAL is available in the LinuxCNC
and HAL User Manuals, found at /usr/share/doc/LinuxCNC/.

.SH BUGS
None known at this time. 
.PP
